expansions={
0:"Notice how changing the prediction unit would change the task. If the unit were a whole delivery zone rather than an individual accepted order, neither the input row nor the target event in this fixture would be the same. Similarly, a horizon of one hour would ask a different question from the stated 30 minutes. Keep unit, decision time, target and horizon in separate record fields so those changes cannot masquerade as implementation details. When reporting 0.30 for the zone, say which zone and which eligible orders provided the denominator. The task definition establishes the interpretation that subsequent dataset and model work must preserve.",
1:"Read the shape from left to right under the declared interpretation: the first length counts observations, and the second counts features within each observation. This tells you where to check batch boundaries and where to check model input width. Do not index shape[1] before establishing rank 2; a flat failure fixture does not have that second axis. Dtype is another independent contract field. An array can have the accepted shape while using the wrong numerical representation, or the accepted dtype while having the wrong axes. Keep those failures distinguishable in tests so fixing one check does not accidentally waive another.",
2:"Inspect a value near a declared precision or range boundary as well as ordinary values. The purpose is to expose the candidate conversion's actual difference from the retained reference, not to assume that every smaller dtype behaves badly or that every successful cast is acceptable. Compare the difference using the fixture's explicit tolerance. A zero difference on one ordinary value is not enough to waive the remaining declared fixtures. Also keep the number of elements unchanged when comparing element bytes; otherwise a reduced total could come from fewer observations instead of a narrower representation. The choice balances measured preservation with the specified storage budget.",
3:"Work through one output row to check meaning as well as compatibility. The first row [2, 10] minus the two feature references [1, 5] becomes [1, 5]. The same reference is then applied to each later observation. A reference operation should express that intended per-feature rule, not simply duplicate an accidental broadcast. For the (3, 1) and (1, 2) case, expanding three row positions against two column positions creates six outputs. That is why validating the output shape matters even when no exception was raised. The check ties the succinct operation to a concrete result rather than treating compact syntax as correctness.",
4:"The listing and the loaded table answer different questions. Listing confirms which objects are available under the authorized location; table inspection confirms how the chosen object's bytes were interpreted. Keep the local path in the retrieval result so a later read cannot accidentally inspect an earlier download. CSV and Parquet should be discussed in terms of the supplied access requirement: text-and-type conversion versus columnar typed access. A selected-column Parquet read does not excuse omitting a column the task needs, just as a CSV conversion does not excuse changing a key's declared representation. Verify the loaded result before calling ingestion complete.",
5:"Treat the arithmetic as a per-chunk admission check. The reader setting proposes an upper row count, but the working matrix's actual shape and dtype determine its element bytes. The final short chunk remains a valid chunk rather than a reason to invent padding rows. Process and emit or summarize that chunk within the declared bounded workflow, then continue without accumulating prior chunks into a full dataset. If the feature width changes, recompute the bound from the actual column count; the old 100-row estimate no longer establishes the same storage requirement. The open file context must encompass the whole iteration, not end before the reader finishes.",
6:"The dictionary should make the observation count and feature count directly accessible under their own names. A caller inspecting a width mismatch should not need to infer it from the means. Likewise, record units or the selected numerical observations beside summaries so a feature's mean is not confused with an average over every number in the matrix. Computing feature-wise summaries over the observation axis produces one result per feature. Keep dtype and element bytes as observed representation properties, distinct from the task's value summaries. A readiness verdict can then be traced to named evidence rather than to an opaque statement that the data was inspected.",
7:"Separate a column-contract failure from a value-contract failure. A missing zone field prevents the declared table schema from being satisfied; a present zone field with an invalid representation is a different reason to reject. The numerical limit test also needs its stated inclusive boundary rather than an assumed strict inequality. Write the failure so the caller can identify the violated condition without guessing from a later estimator exception. Replaying both valid and rejected fixtures verifies that the validator is neither accepting everything nor rejecting everything. Its purpose is to enforce the supplied contract before downstream work depends on that contract.",
8:"A useful cleaning report lets a reviewer trace each affected ID back to the applied policy action. Do not combine ‘repaired’ and ‘rejected’ into an undifferentiated issue count: a repaired record contributes different resulting data from a rejected record. Membership in the accepted-key set is also about the accepted observation history, so follow the supplied action order rather than adding every seen key indiscriminately. The repaired fixture should have its expected resulting values checked, while the duplicate fixture should verify that the prohibited repeat was not accepted. Retain valid observations according to the same policy; defect handling should not replace the dataset's stated purpose.",
9:"Read the ratios as separate conditional questions. The sample's 0.75 zone-A share asks which zone an included observation belongs to. The 0.50 zone-A inclusion probability asks whether a target-population zone-A observation was included. Neither is the target's 0.60 zone-A share. Naming the numerator and denominator in the record prevents a later user from interpreting a selection statistic as population prevalence. The numerical summaries are descriptive evidence for the selected values only. The supported limitation is unequal observed coverage under these supplied counts, not a claim that a particular model must fail or that an unobserved cause of selection has been established.",
10:"Construct the observation-ID and label-ID sets before declaring the join complete. Their differences identify the two unmatched directions: observations without labels and labels without observations. Duplicate IDs need handling before a dictionary silently replaces a value, because set equality alone would not reveal two label rows with the same ID. After the keyed join, inspect the supplied timestamp boundary on the matched record. Key correspondence and time suitability are independent requirements: a correctly keyed label can still be unsuitable under a stated time predicate. This order of checks produces aligned, permitted examples rather than an apparently complete table whose targets belong to another row.",
11:"The set-intersection assertion asks whether the same group identity appears on both sides, not whether two individual order IDs repeat. Distinct observations from G1 can still violate a group boundary. In the time fixture, compare timestamp extrema or the supplied inequalities under the stated cutoff; distinct group sets do not establish temporal ordering. Reporting each partition's target prevalence helps describe what the evaluation cohort actually contains, but it does not choose the boundary retrospectively. Fix the deployment-matched interpretation first, assign observations accordingly and then inspect whether the resulting partitions satisfy it. The evaluation claim must stay tied to that simulated scenario.",
12:"The missing validation row is an application case for the stored statistic. It is not an extra observation from which to relearn the statistic, and the observed value 100 belongs to the held-out cohort rather than the training reference. Check the transformed result and statistics_ together: the expected replacement verifies the output, while unchanged statistics verify reuse of the fitted state. This distinction remains important if the supplied strategy is median, most_frequent or constant instead of mean. The chosen strategy defines how the replacement is learned or supplied; the train-versus-transform boundary defines when its state may change. Preserve both choices in the bounded workflow.",
13:"A validation value beyond the training range can legitimately receive a transformed value beyond the training fixture's transformed values. The value 2 for validation distance 8 follows the fixed formula; it is not a reason to refit until validation has its own mean zero. Verify the column-wise mean and population spread used in the hand calculation, then inspect the fitted parameters corresponding to that feature. Centering and scaling configuration also matters: the stated formula assumes both are enabled. For a constant training feature, report the factor of 1 and the resulting behavior rather than describing an impossible unit-variance transformation. All later cohorts reuse this same fitted interpretation.",
14:"The output width depends on the fitted category set, not on the number of categories occurring in a particular validation batch. Keep columns aligned to the stored training mapping even if a batch contains only north. An unseen east fixture tests the explicit policy without silently extending categories_ during transformation. For the missing fixture, first ask whether missing was represented in the fit data. If yes, its learned indicator follows that mapping; if not, it follows the unknown-category rule. These checks distinguish stable column identity from changing observed batch contents. The metadata dictionary records that identity so the representation remains interpretable to downstream callers.",
15:"Trace a complete prediction call rather than testing transformations and estimation as unrelated pieces. The incoming raw columns are selected, their fitted operations are applied and the resulting representation reaches the final estimator. Intermediate pipeline steps must support fitting and transformation; the final step is the estimator. A manually prepared validation array can accidentally skip a step or use a newly learned category order, which is why the fixture should exercise the fitted workflow's own prediction path. Preserve column assignment and fitted state together. Successful estimation of an already transformed array is not evidence that the raw-input pipeline handles the declared contract correctly.",
16:"Distinguish the prediction-time audit from the held-out-fit audit. The former asks whether each input field could have been known at the declared decision time. The latter asks whether any fitted choice used held-out observations. Removing the eventual-arrival feature addresses the first issue but does not repair a scaler already fitted on validation; splitting before fit addresses the second but does not make a future field available at acceptance. Test both information paths in the bounded fixture. The corrected workflow should produce held-out predictions from training-fitted state and decision-available inputs, not merely show a lower score after deleting a suspicious column.",
17:"Preserve the calculation's order in the code and the test: inspect availability, decide membership, then update the accumulator. Summing every record and later removing a timestamp field would not remove the later record's contribution. Adding the value 7 is a useful invariance test because the earlier prediction boundary has not changed. The historical lookup check is the corresponding question for changing reference state. Both mechanisms enforce the same declared availability boundary, but they concern different inputs to the feature. Retain a boundary fixture for a record at the exact permitted time under the supplied predicate instead of assuming whether equality is included.",
18:"Build a new permitted-field dictionary rather than copying the whole input and hoping no forbidden field remains. The membership rule should use the existing allowed-field collection; adding a field because it appears diagnostically useful would change policy. Inspect both the returned dictionary and the captured output. A removed token field in the returned record does not establish non-disclosure if the input was printed beforehand. Runtime credential delivery and diagnostic-field selection address related but distinct handling paths. Keep the credential reference usable by the permitted runtime while keeping its literal value absent from generated data, metadata, images and logs.",
19:"Walk the confusion table by the question being asked. Precision starts from the predicted-positive group of 15; recall starts from the actual-positive group of 20. FPR instead starts from the actual-negative group, while FNR starts from actual positives. Attaching the relevant counts to a ratio makes it harder to swap these populations. For regression, the same two residuals give different MAE and MSE because squaring changes the aggregation. Choose the declared metric according to target type and error consequences before comparing results. None of these aggregate outcome summaries establishes that individual probability scores match observed outcome frequencies at each score value.",
20:"The expected-cost equation combines conditional error rates with the supplied deployment class probabilities. It does not use validation class proportions as substitutes unless the supplied rule explicitly made them the deployment probabilities. Keep zero cost for correct predictions as a stated assumption; the given equation accounts for the two error terms under that assumption. The latency and operating predicates remain separately named, so an eligibility record can identify exactly which requirement failed. If a conditioning group is empty, report the unresolved rate rather than treating the missing error evidence as perfect performance. Acceptance requirements must remain fixed throughout candidate comparison and final testing.",
23:"The fitted model and validation result have different roles. Fit establishes estimator state from X_train and y_train; predict applies that state to X_validation; evaluation compares those outputs with the corresponding y_validation. Shape agreement is necessary but not enough to establish target correspondence, so use the declared aligned examples. If preprocessing belongs to a fitted pipeline, inspect prediction through that object rather than constructing a fresh validation representation. The resulting baseline is a concrete executable reference under the declared task metric. It is not acceptance evidence until its held-out quantities and required constraints have been calculated and inspected.",
25:"Make exclusions explicit in the ranking record. Excluding C for its different cohort is not the same as measuring C and finding that it loses. Likewise, an operating-limit failure removes eligibility rather than adding an informal penalty to a quality score. The remaining records can be compared under the fixed criterion because their evidence is matched and their decision inputs agree. Retain the selected candidate identity with the calculated quantities and eligibility results, so later stages know precisely which system the validation choice describes. The protected test remains a separate final check after this selection has been frozen.",
26:"Error inspection should preserve the definition of the failure group. The 20 eligible long-distance observations are the population conditioning this ratio; eight is the count of errors within it. Moving the group boundary after reading failures would answer a different question from the predefined slice. Inspect the supplied example failures for supported task limitations, but distinguish observation from causal explanation. A descriptive feature mean or spread can characterize the selected evidence without proving why predictions failed. Keep the same-cohort reference visible so the localized result is comparable rather than a story based only on a few personally chosen examples.",
27:"When presenting slices, keep the group labels, eligible counts and quality definition together. Zone A's 0.05 and zone B's 0.30 are conditional sample results, not interchangeable with overall error. Their denominators also reveal that the two estimates come from different numbers of observations. Report supported limitations in the same terms as the supplied evaluation rather than extrapolating beyond the represented population. Numerical feature summaries describe the selected slice values and need their own observation definition. Slice analysis complements aggregate comparison by exposing where the observed task behavior differs; it does not replace the fixed acceptance rule or prove an unmeasured population effect.",
28:"The multiplication by 0.25 is the population weighting step, not a revision to the subgroup's conditional rate. Keep subgroup false-positive and false-negative conditions distinct when computing its harm. Then compare the supplied mitigation with the reference on a matched affected segment and overall cohort. An improvement in the subgroup contribution is useful evidence only under the supplied population probability and cost assumptions. Inspect representation before extending that evidence to deployment. The exercise is a bounded check of a provided mitigation; it does not authorize inventing protected categories, new policies or an untested repair that merely seems fair.",
30:"Retain the trial's seed and baseline/candidate results in the same record so the win calculation can be reconstructed pair by pair. A mean over candidate results and a separate mean over baseline results may summarize levels, but it does not retain which matched trials were wins. The supplied seed protocol also governs splits where applicable, not only the estimator. Report the empirical 0.60 alongside the five completed pairs and the declared spread calculation. This bounded evidence supports a repeatability comparison while leaving unsupported environmental or computation-wide determinism claims unresolved.",
31:"The validation comparison remains fixed as you vary the supplied regularization setting. Do not quietly change cost assumptions, cohorts or a different estimator parameter at the same time. A training/validation gap under comparable score definitions is evidence about generalization worth investigating; the chosen setting is selected from its validation evidence and required limits. Keep estimator names beside alpha or C so their opposite penalty-direction interpretations are unambiguous. The protected-test boundary applies to regularization just as it does to model choice. A final test result cannot become an extra trial in this tuning comparison.",
32:"A completed-trial record should retain the actual configuration passed to fit, not only the search space from which it came. That makes a keyword budget override and a selected setting independently inspectable. A grid with more combinations than the intended bounded procedure requires the supplied execution rule rather than an assumed unlimited run. The validation protocol determines the scoring population, while the search mechanism determines which configurations are tried. Keep those roles distinct when inspecting best_params_ and cv_results_. The selected result is still subject to the predeclared eligibility requirements rather than automatically approved because the search labels it best.",
33:"Use policy language for permissions and evidence language for limitations. An observed grant mismatch is compared with the allowed identity set; it is not repaired by expanding that set in the documentation. A supported segment limitation belongs to the evaluation record and should be described at that scope. A credential-handling issue can be identified through the field or location concerned without reproducing the value. Preserve the task's foreseeable misuse cases and stated permitted use alongside the observed facts. This separation prevents the record from becoming either a new authorization policy or an unsupported claim of suitability.",
34:"Alignment is the first comparison requirement: each supplied output must belong to the labeled observation whose outcome is evaluated. The fixed metric and deployment-cost assumptions are the next requirements, followed by the existing acceptance limits. A favorable result on these supplied examples is bounded evidence for this task and cohort, not a statement about every foundation model or application. Report limitations in the same evaluation terms. The point of the exercise is to read and compare an existing output record accurately without crossing into the separately owned mechanisms for building prompts, retrieval workflows or new applications.",
35:"Inspect features and targets separately before checking their common observation axis. A classification target representation may differ from numerical features, so an explicit cast should use the target's declared dtype rather than a shared convenience setting. Return the pair only after the axes and representations satisfy the contract. In the three-target failure fixture, tensor conversion may still succeed; the alignment check is what rejects it. Test that failure alongside an accepted pair and the supplied boundary. This establishes a reliable input contract for later minibatch use without relying on a subsequent loss to expose an earlier conversion error.",
36:"Indexing defines correspondence before batching. If __getitem__ uses the feature at one index and the target at another, a loader can still collate a well-shaped but incorrectly paired batch. Test item identities as well as batch dimensions. The five-observation fixture also exposes the final partial-batch policy: retaining it gives one smaller batch, while dropping it changes how much of the dataset is consumed. Shuffle governs order, not whether a feature and its target remain the same item. Keep these responsibilities distinct so the expected loader output is tied to the dataset contract rather than assumed from its shape alone.",
37:"Draw or inspect the dimension chain for a single observation and then restore the leading minibatch dimension. Two features enter the first layer, three intermediate values emerge and one final output is produced; all four observations follow the same chain. Registered layer attributes make those layer parameters part of the module. The activation is elementwise, so it changes values without changing that intermediate width. Finally, compare the model output with the declared target/loss contract. The architecture example remains bounded to that contract rather than adding layers or final nonlinearities simply because they appear in another task.",
38:"Read the matrix reference one parameter at a time. The first weight combines feature values 1 and 3 with derivatives 0.1 and 0.2, giving 0.7. The second combines 2 and 4 with the same derivatives, giving 1.0. The bias combines derivatives over rows, giving 0.3. These shapes are part of the check: a transpose error can yield a different object even when some scalar values look plausible. Because D includes the loss reduction, use it once as supplied. Compare after backward and before clearing so the inspected gradients correspond to the intended fresh computation rather than zeroed or accumulated state.",
39:"Keep the mean-reduction factor visible in each reference. The two-element MSE fixture divides squared errors by two, while the one-element binary-logit fixture divides its sigmoid-minus-target derivative by one. A class-index cross-entropy reference subtracts the one-hot target from the softmax vector and divides by the sample count. Those equations support different target representations, so verify target dtype and axes before applying them. A positive-looking scalar loss is not proof of the right contract. Compare both value and derivative direction in the bounded fixture, retaining the supplied assumptions about unweighted mean reduction.",
40:"Retain the current gradient separately from the observed parameter change. The former is produced by backward; the latter is produced by step acting on the parameters bound to the optimizer. A parameter change of −0.3 matches the plain-SGD reference for gradient 3 and rate 0.1, but the same number alone would not identify what happened if those inputs differed. Check before/after values and declared tolerances together. Clearing gradients before the next backward prevents previous contributions from altering the intended fresh-step reference. Keep this one-step verification bounded to the stated optimizer configuration rather than extending its equation to Adam.",
41:"Loss aggregation needs the accompanying batch counts because the last one-observation batch does not contribute the same number of examples as a two-observation batch. Record each scalar with its batch size before applying the declared epoch-summary rule. The loop's nested structure is equally important: each epoch iterates its loader, and each minibatch performs the complete current-gradient update sequence. A step outside the intended minibatch position would define a different training procedure. The deterministic fixture can inspect one update within the loop, making the control flow and parameter-change evidence meet at the same minibatch.",
43:"The state mapping and prediction fixture provide complementary checks. Corresponding entries show whether learned parameter values survived persistence; matching fixed-fixture outputs show whether the compatible restored architecture uses them as expected in evaluation mode. An output coincidence on a single example does not replace entry checks. Keep the original prediction reference until after reload instead of computing both references with the restored object. Binary file handles are required for the specified save/load path. The checkpoint is learned state for the supplied architecture, not a license to substitute a differently shaped model and treat a successful file read as restoration.",
44:"Trace the controller's counter explicitly after every validation value. Reset only when the minimized quantity improves by more than min_delta, increment otherwise and stop when patience is exhausted or the epoch bound is reached. The fixture's small decrease from 0.44 to 0.43 is intentionally insufficient under the declared 0.02 rule. Save or deep-copy the monitored best weights at the intended improvement point. This separates controller state from the live model state that later epochs can change. Restore that saved checkpoint for subsequent use rather than the last weights merely because they were the most recently trained.",
45:"The identical rerun is what makes the correction test informative. Preserve the fixture, target contract and baseline failing evidence while changing the one supported factor. If the correction is intended to restore a missing gradient path, inspect the derivative and parameter .grad at the same points as before. If the supplied cause concerns representation or learning rate, retain those resolved inputs in the comparison. Record whether the corrected bounded task meets its declared expectations, not just whether an exception disappeared. This isolates evidence for one hypothesis without claiming that all future training failures have the same cause.",
47:"Changing batch size changes both a storage estimate and the number of examples grouped into each update, so hold the supplied task and comparison protocol fixed. Record the actual batch shapes, peak measurement boundary and completed-example count. A final incomplete batch needs its own count rather than the configured maximum. The CUDA peak statistic should be reset for each trial so a previous larger batch does not remain the reported peak for the new setting. Select among settings that meet the declared memory and performance requirements, retaining the distinction between input estimates and measured allocated tensor storage.",
49:"The profiler trace supplies attribution, while the unprofiled rerun supplies the matched elapsed-time comparison. Keep the same bounded workload and one-factor change between those two comparisons. A loading-region label should enclose the intended loading work; a model-compute label should identify that separate work rather than blend it with setup. Runtime CPU, memory and process evidence must refer to the same window. Synchronization at accelerator timing boundaries accounts for asynchronous completion. This makes the observed difference interpretable without assuming that a profiler's overhead or a shifted measurement boundary is a genuine speed improvement.",
54:"The parsed manifest is the artifact a later execution will read, so inspect it after serialization rather than only inspecting the in-memory dictionary that preceded writing. Compare its dependency mapping with the freeze output, its revision with HEAD and its Python/runtime fields with the actual process. Paths such as sys.executable help identify which interpreter executed, while sys.version records that interpreter's version information. Keep these values beside the environment identity instead of treating them as substitutes for it. A mismatch is a verification failure to resolve, not a reason to change the independently observed environment values.",
58:"Freeze means the choices are made before test outcomes are observed: model identity, fitted preprocessing, threshold, metric inputs and requirements all retain their declared values. The baseline and candidate predictions then use the same protected observations for a final matched comparison. Retain the test's observed conditioning counts while applying the supplied deployment probabilities; these are different roles in the calculation. If a required quantity is undefined or a requirement fails, report that outcome explicitly. This protects the interpretation of final testing rather than using it as a source of additional tuning information.",
62:"Keep an output key beside its prediction through serialization, not merely in a temporary input structure. After writing, decode the fixture and compare key coverage against the eligible input IDs. A duplicate result for A plus a missing result for B could leave the total row count unchanged, which is why correspondence needs more than counting rows. Each chunk uses the same fitted objects and declared response schema. The bounded writer and reader handles establish where results were produced and re-inspected. This completes an inference path whose correctness includes persistence and identity, not only in-memory prediction values.",
69:"Use a timeline for the same identified request to avoid measuring different intervals under different settings. Start-to-response timing includes the waiting interval, and the selected successful-response population determines which durations enter the percentile. Record the sample count, units and percentile convention so the numerical summary is reproducible. A limit that reduces model-execution time but increases waiting may fail the full latency objective. The supplied trace is evidence about those measured settings and eligible responses; it does not authorize inventing an unmeasured batching configuration or treating unmatched responses as valid duration samples.",
79:"Walk the identity chain in order, comparing deployment to registry, registry to artifact/run, run to recorded configuration and dataset, and code record to the existing commit. Each edge can fail independently, so preserve the missing or mismatched link instead of collapsing every result into a plausible name. The exact-generation download checks content against the lineage record, while local revision inspection checks whether the referenced code exists. Together they make provenance auditable from supplied records. They do not recover an absent lineage link by guesswork, even when deployment and experiment names look similar.",
80:"Fixed bins make numerical proportions refer to the same intervals in both windows. The eligible denominator also matters if values outside the declared eligible set are handled explicitly by the reference constraints. For categories, preserve declared category definitions and count every declared category so an absent current category still has a position in the aligned comparison. Means and standard deviations describe selected numerical observations with their specified divisor. Retain these summaries together with window and reference identity. That record supports investigating what distribution changed without silently redefining the measurement between reference and production.",
81:"Separate an operational report into what is observed and what is unresolved. More long-distance inputs support an input-distribution statement. Matched labels compared with the quality reference support an observed-error statement. Conditional-target evidence addresses whether the feature/label relationship changed. The absence of labels does not prove that quality stayed constant; it means the labeled-quality question is not yet measured by that evidence. Likewise, input drift does not prove that quality worsened. Keeping these distinctions preserves uncertainty without discarding useful distribution or service evidence, and prevents a response justified by one type of evidence from being mislabeled as another.",
82:"The same reference/current vectors can give a decision only under the declared distance or significance rule. Record the equation's resolved inputs and criterion beside its verdict, rather than showing a bare alert with no comparison definition. Each window's proportions use its own eligible total, so unequal sample sizes do not mean raw count differences are themselves the drift quantity. Numerical summaries retain the stated mean and spread conventions. Report feature-level crossings under that rule and preserve the separate question of labeled model quality. This makes the detection reproducible without claiming a causal performance effect.",
83:"Preserve cohort membership before labels arrive so later analysis cannot redefine the cohort around whichever predictions happened to receive labels. The availability boundary determines which matched labels are mature for this analysis. Duplicate labels or prediction IDs require explicit handling before the dictionary can conceal them. Report the 60 mature IDs and 100 eligible IDs alongside the six matched errors. The 0.10 result describes the mature matched cohort, while 0.60 describes its label coverage. These different ratios should not be merged into an all-traffic quality estimate without justified coverage evidence.",
85:"Test the selected hypothesis against evidence that can distinguish it from alternatives. An artifact mismatch supports a different investigation from a schema defect, and neither is established merely by a distribution difference. Matched mature-label rates need their own release/cohort counts, so incomplete labels are not treated as successful predictions. Keep the incident response within the existing policy and its authorization boundary. After choosing the supported data repair, rollback or retraining path, preserve the corresponding validation gates and audit evidence. The diagnosis is bounded to the reproduced regression and available evidence rather than a blanket explanation of all model errors.",
90:"The pre-recovery evidence is important because stop/start can change process state and remove the immediate fault symptom. Inspect the authorized instance before acting, record what failed and test the runbook's supported hypothesis. After start completes, reconnect and compare model-service state and endpoint behavior with the expected contract. A running instance state is a lifecycle observation; readiness and a successful bounded prediction are service observations. Retain both in the same recovery record along with authorized target identity. This verifies the supplied recovery procedure without assuming that a restart of an arbitrary resource would be safe or sufficient.",
91:"Resource samples need both units and identity. CPU percent and memory units are not interchangeable columns, and their descriptive summaries should cover the same matched workload interval. The lifecycle record helps distinguish a stopped instance from an active measurement window. Process inspection adds evidence that the workload named in the report was actually running. Keep observation counts visible for both series and use the stated standard-deviation divisor. These summaries characterize resource usage during the bounded task; they do not independently establish billed cost, request success or model quality.",
}
# Add a second paragraph to the example, not a new concept or repeated rule card.
for i,text in expansions.items():
    intro,example,contrast,level,mode,reason=cases[i]
    cases[i]=(intro,example+'\n\n'+text,contrast,level,mode,reason)
